A||||4||SKIDMARK||Custom Paint My Engine!||||6||
Z||000000||SKIDMARK||10-18-2001||09:14 AM||||I just got a low mileage 3.4 yesterday and decided I would dress it up before I put it in. Does anyone know if there is such a thing as high temp paint that comes in custom colors? If not, what kind of paint did you use and with what kind of success/failure. I was thinking like school bus yellow and maybe radar blue. Also, is there any way to keep the paint from burning off the heads around the exhaust ports? <P>------------------<BR>White '85 4cyl coupe<BR>Black '86 v-6 SE<BR>'81 CB900F Super Sport||||reg||6
Z||000001||StuGood||10-18-2001||01:03 PM||||Stimpy's engine was painted yellow (plenum and valve covers, at least, if I remember correctly), and from the pictures he has posted, it looks very sharp.  He used powder coating... something to think about; might be more colors available to choose from.  Maybe he can comment on the durability?<P>As far as keeping paint on the headers, FWIW, I used some silver "500-degree" spraypaint on my aft manifold, and silver "1200-degree" spraypaint on my forward manifold.  So I'm inadvertently conducting a comparison test, here.<P>The aft's ("500-degree") paint started to bubble / lose paint almost immediately.  The forward's ("1200-degree") paint I haven't  checked on, but I can tell you that it was a lot shinier than the 500-degree stuff.  That's all I know.      ||||reg||1
Z||000002||qwikgta||10-18-2001||11:22 PM||||You have to use at least 1000 degree paint on manifolds.  I too used 500' paint on my header and it was smoking in about 5 seconds.  I used 1200' paint next and it has been fine.<P>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||10-18-2001||11:40 PM||||Here is my 3.4 painted with high temp paint......<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/engine3_1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/engine4.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocks_sig.jpg">    </A><BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mach10||10-19-2001||12:12 AM||||Don't have any photos, but the motor we're buying (waiting for the guy to rip it out) for the Raider has the block powder-coated in BRIGHT PINK.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><P>'cos he calls his Mitsu-Montero "The Pig"||||reg||10
